{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["יַלְדְתִּיהוּ — ילד את אלמודד — he has given birth to others; therefore Scripture may say: וירשתם אותם." "יְלִדְתִּיהוּ — both with a hirek, because from their respective binyanim it resembles a hiphil-like (מפעיל) pattern. But ישב, which belongs to the person's own body, gives וִישַׁבְתֶּם. יָשֵׁן — וְיָשַׁנְתֶּם. All their counterparts are open (ptach). And likewise from ירד — וְיָרַדְתֶּם."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The comment appears to address the unusual hiphil form ילדתיהו by citing another hiphil form (הוליד/ילד את) and then drawing a grammatical inference; the precise logic connecting to וירשתם אותם is unclear and the text may be corrupt or elliptical.", 1 "The grammatical argument is compressed and partially obscure; 'both with a hirek' likely refers to the consonantal spelling or vocalization shared by related forms. The contrast between hiphil-like forms and intransitive forms with ptach (paal) counterparts is rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:50:08.970739038Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}